use  in the snowy mountains peter zundtos  style  it really didn't do the job now look  don't get me wrong this is still really  really good work but at the end of the  day it's not a circle house it's not  really in the peters until style and  it's kind of very mundane last but not  least is oscar nehemiah oscar nehemiah  is personally one of my favorite  architects and i use as inspiration for  my work all of the time so when i asked  the ai to produce a future utopian house  oscar nemai style 8k hyper realistic it  was able to take some of oscar neymar's  work basically extrapolate it and turn  it into the modern day version of a  house which is exactly what i asked for  but very much copy and pasting one  project into another which is basically  plagiarism now if we analyze this ai  from a pros and cons list it gets pretty  simple first of all it is quick it's  easy to use it is great for ideas it can  produce amazing results in any style and  it is forever learning so it's forever  getting better however the ai seems to  latch onto one word the mid-journey  version only lets you use 25  imaginations of your own before it asks  you to subscribe to its paid service if  you're trying to describe multiple ideas  in one image it really starts to  struggle and it also adds up over time  so if you're trying to produce one image  it may take 30 seconds it may take 3  minutes to generate this image but 10  images is half an hour 100 images goes  on for a very very long time i still  don't think this software is 100 ready  for full mass market adoption but it is  getting very very close the invitation  only services like dali e  are phenomenal and that's what takes us  to our very next point i promise that  i'll tell you exactly how you can get  unlimited access to ai 100 free like i  already said mid journey only allows you  25 imaginations and then it asks you to  subscribe  mid journey is actually really really  good because it allows you to upscale  these images it allows you to get high  resolution data of what you're actually  trying to produce  however if you're just experimenting  with the program you can use something  called crayon which is the original dali  e software it's called dali e mini and  it allows you to produce very scaled  down versions of the concepts  unfortunately you cannot scale up you're  basically just screenshotting images so  you're not able to actually blow these  images up and use them for anything but  they're great for idea creation anyway  that's all from me if you enjoyed the  content make sure you check out the  everything architecture playlist on the  side of me here and if you love the  content make sure you smash the  subscribe button down below but like  always i'll see you next monday
 

